{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"slug\":\"canada-monthly-gdp-growth-november-2026\",\"country\":\"CA\",\"type\":\"data\",\"title\":\"Canada monthly GDP growth, November 2026\",\"question\":\"Statistics Canada GDP by industry, all industries, Canada, seasonally adjusted at annual rates, chained 2017 dollars: November 2026 first-print month-over-month percent growth from vector v65201210.\",\"unit\":\"percent_growth\",\"pointEstimate\":0.1,\"ciLow\":-0.27,\"ciHigh\":0.47,\"confidence\":0.8,\"resolutionDate\":\"2027-01-29\",\"resolutionSource\":\"Statistics Canada GDP by industry table 36-10-0434-01 / WDS vector v65201210\",\"resolutionSourceUrl\":\"https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/t1/wds/rest/getDataFromVectorByReferencePeriodRange?vectorIds=%2265201210%22&startRefPeriod=2026-10-01&endReferencePeriod=2026-11-01\",\"resolutionRule\":\"On the first official Statistics Canada print scheduled for 2027-01-29, read vector v65201210 for all industries, Canada, seasonally adjusted at annual rates, chained 2017 dollars, in table 36-10-0434-01. Compute 100*(November 2026 level - October 2026 level)/October 2026 level in percent_growth. Use that first print only; ignore later revisions and do not add same-day correction or release-day grace exceptions.\",\"dataPointId\":\"statcan.gdp_by_industry.monthly_growth.2026_11.first_print\",\"historicalContext\":[{\"period\":{\"type\":\"month\",\"value\":\"2026-03\"},\"label\":\"March 2026\",\"value\":-0.1521},{\"period\":{\"type\":\"month\",\"value\":\"2026-04\"},\"label\":\"April 2026\",\"value\":0.6326},{\"period\":{\"type\":\"month\",\"value\":\"2026-05\"},\"label\":\"May 2026\",\"value\":0.3415},{\"period\":{\"type\":\"month\",\"value\":\"2026-06\"},\"label\":\"June 2026\",\"value\":0.3512},{\"period\":{\"type\":\"month\",\"value\":\"2026-07\"},\"label\":\"July 2026\",\"value\":0.0258},{\"period\":{\"type\":\"month\",\"value\":\"2026-08\"},\"label\":\"August 2026\",\"value\":-0.0065}],\"drivers\":[\"Recent official monthly GDP growth averaged about 0.20% across March-August 2026 on current WDS levels.\",\"Latest The Daily release says August was essentially unchanged and the advance September estimate was -0.1%.\",\"Momentum is softer than the six-month mean, but November is two months beyond the last official print and likely mean-reverts toward small positive growth.\",\"One-off industry rebounds in April-June raise historical volatility but are not assumed to persist into November.\"],\"sourceContext\":[\"https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/t1/wds/rest/getDataFromVectorByReferencePeriodRange?vectorIds=%2265201210%22&startRefPeriod=2025-10-01&endReferencePeriod=2026-10-01\",\"https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/n1/release-diffusion/2026-eng.pdf\",\"https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/n1/daily-quotidien/261030/dq261030a-eng.htm\",\"https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/n1/pub/13-607-x/2016001/v65201210-eng.htm\"],\"runAt\":\"2026-11-02T23:43:33Z\",\"reasoning\":[{\"kind\":\"heading\",\"text\":\"Canada November 2026 monthly GDP by industry first print\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The target is the Statistics Canada all-industries GDP by industry level series v65201210, seasonally adjusted at annual rates, chained 2017 dollars, transformed to month-over-month percent growth for November 2026. I verified the 2026-2027 Statistics Canada major economic releases schedule captured in call-0005: Gross domestic product by industry for reference period November 2026 is scheduled for January 29, 2027.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"fetch_source call-0004 read StatCan WDS vector v65201210 for 2025-10 through 2026-08\",\"result\":\"Fetched official levels included February 2026 = 2343599.0, March 2026 = 2340035.0, April 2026 = 2354837.0, May 2026 = 2362878.0, June 2026 = 2371177.0, July 2026 = 2371788.0, and August 2026 = 2371635.0.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"evidence.calculate\",\"call\":\"calculate calls call-0018 through call-0023 transformed the fetched v65201210 levels into month-over-month percent changes\",\"result\":\"Computed changes from fetched levels were March -0.1521%, April 0.6326%, May 0.3415%, June 0.3512%, July 0.0258%, and August -0.0065%.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"fetch_source call-0006 read The Daily release for Gross domestic product by industry, August 2026\",\"result\":\"The captured Statistics Canada release reports August 2026 real GDP was essentially unchanged, consistent with 2371788.0 to 2371635.0 or -0.0065%, and gives an advance September 2026 estimate of -0.1%.\"},{\"kind\":\"math\",\"text\":\"Prior/update/interval: I use a persistence/base rate prior from the official-source reference class of six recent monthly growth observations, March-August 2026, with mean = 0.1987% from call-0025. I adjust downward for soft late-summer momentum and the -0.1% advance September signal, landing at 0.10% for November rather than the raw 0.20% mean. For the 80% interval, sigma = 0.2922 from call-0024 using the six growth values themselves; 1.28*sigma = 0.3740 from call-0026, so 0.10 +/- 0.374 gives -0.2740 to 0.4740, rounded to -0.27 to 0.47.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Level, momentum, one-off, and policy mechanisms: the level trend is mildly positive over the six official observations, momentum is near flat after July-August and the advance September estimate, one-off rebounds in mining/manufacturing can move a monthly print but are not persistent, and there is no policy-decision mechanism in this data target.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Upside risk is a broad rebound in goods sectors or resource extraction that would land above the interval. Downside risk is another contraction in manufacturing, mining, or tariff-sensitive trade channels that would land below the interval. Outside the interval would require a roughly larger-than-0.47% expansion or worse-than--0.27% contraction, larger than the normal recent monthly dispersion except for the April rebound.\"},{\"kind\":\"forecast\",\"point\":0.1,\"ciLow\":-0.27,\"ciHigh\":0.47}]}"}}
